# examples\kalk\kalk.banks -- the file browser lives in a RAM bank.
#
# filepick is ~3 KB of library code that a spreadsheet only touches
# while the panel is up, and kalk is within a few KB of the low-RAM
# ceiling. Banked, its wrappers page bank 20 in, call, and page back;
# what is left in low RAM is the handful of bytes for those wrappers.
#
# dir is not listed and must not be: the library forces X16_USE_DIR on
# wherever X16_USE_FILEPICK is on, so dir is assembled into the bank
# image alongside the browser that calls it -- naming it here only earns
# a "matches no module used by this program" warning, because kalk never
# calls a dir_* routine itself. screen, float, fileio and the rest stay
# in low RAM: those are kalk's inner loops.
#
#   .\build.ps1 examples\kalk\kalk.p8 -BankFile examples\kalk\kalk.banks
#
# (examples\kalk\build.ps1 passes this file for you.)
#
# dos joins them: asking the drive why a load failed is not worth
# 300 bytes of low RAM, and the browser already needs it in there.
# mouse joins them so the diagnostics fit: kalk polls the mouse once per
# loop, so it does not mind the far call. number used to be here too,
# but kalk formats through float now and calls nothing from it.
bank 20, "filepick,dos,mouse"
